gpui: Carry out a web view's focus() and blur()

Against longbridge/nsh e626a8d (0.4.0). WebViewRef.focus() and blur()
reached text_input::focus / blur, which only know text fields, and
WebItem::command dropped Command::Focus / Command::Blur, so an app could
never give a WKWebView the keyboard or take it back. Focus / Blur on a
web view now go to the web view: focus() makes it the window's first
responder (wry's WebView::focus, guarded because it unwraps the view's
window), blur() hands first responder back to the surface's view
(wry's focus_parent). On focus the app's focused field is blurred and a
pending window-focus request is dropped, so the next frame does not
take the keyboard straight back. SendInput is still not handled.

